WEBVTT

00:00:45.546 --> 00:00:48.966
<i>Kokoro egakidasu</i>

00:00:48.966 --> 00:00:52.386
<i>chizujou no michinaru frontier</i>

00:00:52.386 --> 00:00:55.806
<i>Tobira hiraitara</i>

00:00:55.806 --> 00:00:59.142
<i>michi wa tsuzuiteiru yo</i>

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:05.107
<i>Hokori makiagete kimi no machi e</i>

00:01:05.107 --> 00:01:11.822
<i>Sora to daichi ga kasanaru ruuto de</i>

00:01:11.822 --> 00:01:15.576
<i>Hashiru minamikaze ni notte</i>

00:01:15.576 --> 00:01:18.495
<i>Aoku somaru kaze wo kitte</i>

00:01:18.495 --> 00:01:25.627
<i>Kokorogoto kakedashiteirun da</i>

00:01:25.627 --> 00:01:29.298
<i>Mahiru no tsuki wo oikoshite</i>

00:01:29.298 --> 00:01:32.259
<i>Kinou to wa chigau sekai e</i>

00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:37.681
<i>Dokomademo hashirinuketeku</i>

00:01:37.681 --> 00:01:41.602
<i>Ano kaze no you ni</i>

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:46.899
<i>Ano kaze no you ni</i>

00:01:59.494 --> 00:02:00.412
"Merida Island"

00:02:00.412 --> 00:02:03.624
Argos 4, this is Merida final controller.

00:02:03.624 --> 00:02:06.668
Your heading looks good.
On course. On glide path.

00:02:06.668 --> 00:02:09.838
This is Argos 4.
I have visual on the runway.

00:02:09.838 --> 00:02:12.257
Argos 4, you have
permission to land.

00:02:24.478 --> 00:02:28.690
"Jungle Groove"

00:02:36.949 --> 00:02:38.909
First Lieutenant,
please sign here.

00:02:38.909 --> 00:02:40.327
Sure.

00:02:45.457 --> 00:02:48.377
Shall I have your luggage
sent directly to your room?

00:02:48.377 --> 00:02:50.712
Thanks. Please do.

00:02:50.712 --> 00:02:52.047
Yes, sir.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:20.742
Yes?

00:03:20.742 --> 00:03:24.079
Captain, Sergeant Sagara has arrived.

00:03:24.079 --> 00:03:25.247
Please send him in.

00:03:25.247 --> 00:03:26.290
Yes, ma'am.

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:32.254
Come in.

00:03:33.255 --> 00:03:34.923
Excuse me.

00:03:40.262 --> 00:03:44.224
Sergeant Sousuke Sagara
has returned to normal duties.

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:47.227
Good work.
At ease.

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:49.062
Yes, Captain.

00:03:55.569 --> 00:03:58.197
Did you say goodbye to
Miss Kaname before you left?

00:03:58.197 --> 00:04:00.365
No, ma'am.

00:04:00.365 --> 00:04:03.744
You must have something
you would like to say to me.

00:04:03.744 --> 00:04:05.829
No, ma'am. Nothing.

00:04:05.829 --> 00:04:07.998
Calling you back from Tokyo

00:04:07.998 --> 00:04:10.459
was a decision made by both
Tactical Headquarters and myself.

00:04:10.459 --> 00:04:12.544
Because preparations
have already been completed

00:04:12.544 --> 00:04:16.548
to have an Intelligence agent permanently
stationed around Miss Kaname.

00:04:16.548 --> 00:04:19.968
What about document file 05B-D113?

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:21.428
What are you talking about?

00:04:21.428 --> 00:04:23.305
My report.

00:04:23.305 --> 00:04:28.977
I have explained repeatedly that Intelligence
has not been guarding her sufficiently.

00:04:28.977 --> 00:04:31.480
That is strictly your own impression.

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:34.441
Are you saying you question my report?

00:04:34.441 --> 00:04:37.361
I said no such thing. It was one
of many materials used to decide...

00:04:37.361 --> 00:04:39.321
I am suitable to guard her.

00:04:39.321 --> 00:04:42.324
Or at least that's what I thought, Captain.

00:04:42.324 --> 00:04:47.287
It seems you do not understand
your own place, Sergeant.

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:50.499
You have other duties on which
you should focus, do you not?

00:04:50.499 --> 00:04:51.959
And what duties would those be?

00:04:51.959 --> 00:04:53.293
The Arbalest.

00:04:54.545 --> 00:04:57.464
You are to give your undivided
attention to operating that machine.

00:04:57.464 --> 00:04:58.882
During that hijacking incident,

00:04:58.882 --> 00:05:01.176
the Arbalest ended up being optimized
for the first person to get into it.

00:05:01.176 --> 00:05:04.179
In other words, you.

00:05:04.179 --> 00:05:09.560
The developer has died, so we are
unable to change that setting.

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:11.395
Through trial and error,
the only thing we discovered

00:05:11.395 --> 00:05:16.650
was that the Arbalest's Lambda Driver
will not activate for anyone except you.

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:17.609
On the other hand,

00:05:17.609 --> 00:05:21.947
Amalgam or whoever they are has utilized
the same type of machine numerous times.

00:05:21.947 --> 00:05:24.616
It was the same in
Nanking the other day.

00:05:24.616 --> 00:05:27.244
The only ones who can counter a machine
equipped with a Lambda Driver

00:05:27.244 --> 00:05:29.371
are you and the Arbalest.

00:05:31.248 --> 00:05:34.251
You are to leave the guarding
of Miss Kaname up to Intelligence,

00:05:34.251 --> 00:05:37.921
and devote yourself to mastering
the use of that machine.

00:05:40.549 --> 00:05:43.051
Are you saying I have no choice?

00:05:43.051 --> 00:05:44.511
Yes.

00:05:44.511 --> 00:05:47.139
Please understand, Mr. Sagara.

00:05:47.139 --> 00:05:49.433
Is that an order?

00:05:54.855 --> 00:05:57.524
Yes, it is.

00:05:57.524 --> 00:05:59.526
If that's what it takes to satisfy you,

00:05:59.526 --> 00:06:01.612
I'll give you an order
or do anything else,

00:06:01.612 --> 00:06:05.866
even if that means taking
you away from Miss Kaname.

00:06:05.866 --> 00:06:08.118
You have it so easy, don't you?

00:06:08.118 --> 00:06:11.079
Because you can distract yourself
by holding a grudge against me.

00:06:11.079 --> 00:06:15.083
But I have to consider
the safety of my subordinates!

00:06:15.083 --> 00:06:16.960
You know how powerful
the enemy is, don't you?

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:20.589
Melissa might die next time!
And so might Mr. Weber!

00:06:20.589 --> 00:06:26.178
Do you have any idea what it's like
for me to be sitting in the captain's chair?!

00:06:26.178 --> 00:06:27.930
What are you looking at?

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:30.057
Is she the only thing
running through your head?

00:06:30.057 --> 00:06:32.893
Have you thought about
my feelings even a little bit?

00:06:32.893 --> 00:06:33.936
I...

00:06:33.936 --> 00:06:35.771
You disgust me!

00:06:35.771 --> 00:06:37.564
You always pretend
to be obedient and kind,

00:06:37.564 --> 00:06:39.900
but you're actually cruel
and self-centered, aren't you?!

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:42.236
Not only that,
you're lying to yourself!

00:06:42.236 --> 00:06:45.030
Why don't you just
come right out and say it?

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:48.200
"I want to be with her!
Don't get in the way!"

00:06:50.994 --> 00:06:55.999
It would have been so much easier
if you had just said that.

00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:12.140
Yes?

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:14.935
Captain, First Lieutenant Clouseau
is here to see you.

00:07:14.935 --> 00:07:18.981
Please have him wait for a moment.
I will call him in shortly.

00:07:18.981 --> 00:07:20.274
Yes, ma'am.

00:07:22.317 --> 00:07:24.528
I hate you, Mr. Sagara.

00:07:24.528 --> 00:07:25.529
I'm sorry.

00:07:25.529 --> 00:07:29.366
I hate that you're always
quick to apologize, too.

00:07:29.366 --> 00:07:30.909
I'm truly sorry.

00:07:32.286 --> 00:07:34.538
I have nothing more
to speak to you about.

00:07:34.538 --> 00:07:35.914
Dismissed.

00:07:35.914 --> 00:07:36.957
Yes, ma'am.

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:48.302
Who was that officer just now?

00:07:48.302 --> 00:07:51.388
Sergeant Sagara, a member
of the Special Response Team.

00:07:53.056 --> 00:07:54.016
Yes, ma'am?

00:07:55.642 --> 00:07:58.395
Thank you for waiting.
You can go in now, First Lieutenant.

00:07:58.395 --> 00:07:59.605
Thanks.

00:08:03.233 --> 00:08:07.404
First Lieutenant Belfangan Clouseau,
reporting for duty as of today.

00:08:07.404 --> 00:08:11.950
Welcome to the West Pacific Fleet,
First Lieutenant. At ease.

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:13.118
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:13.118 --> 00:08:15.954
I am familiar with your
military fame, Captain.

00:08:15.954 --> 00:08:17.581
I am honored to meet you.

00:08:17.581 --> 00:08:19.041
Same here.

00:08:19.041 --> 00:08:21.585
Have you met your new subordinates?

00:08:21.585 --> 00:08:23.504
I have not talked with them yet.

00:08:23.504 --> 00:08:27.049
Instead of introductions,
there is something I want to test.

00:08:27.049 --> 00:08:28.634
Something you want to test?

00:08:28.634 --> 00:08:31.512
It may be a little rough, though.

00:08:33.347 --> 00:08:36.016
So you made her cry, then?

00:08:36.016 --> 00:08:37.017
Yeah.

00:08:37.017 --> 00:08:38.310
I'm impressed!

00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:41.688
You actually might have some
talent as a gigolo, you know?

00:08:41.688 --> 00:08:43.357
What's a gigolo?

00:08:43.357 --> 00:08:46.985
Don't worry about it.
But anyway...

00:08:46.985 --> 00:08:49.279
I don't know what to say, man.

00:08:49.279 --> 00:08:50.739
You certainly seem
to be enjoying yourself.

00:08:50.739 --> 00:08:53.075
Yup, pretty much.

00:08:54.451 --> 00:08:57.037
The captain's assertion was correct.

00:08:57.037 --> 00:09:00.749
There's certainly no reason for me
to be compelled to guard Chidori.

00:09:00.749 --> 00:09:03.669
If you think in terms of putting
the right person in the right post,

00:09:03.669 --> 00:09:06.505
the measures Mithril has taken concerning
Chidori up until now probably are odd.

00:09:06.505 --> 00:09:09.716
Well, I guess it was
absurd to begin with.

00:09:09.716 --> 00:09:11.343
Yeah, but...

00:09:11.343 --> 00:09:12.553
But?

00:09:12.553 --> 00:09:14.054
Logically, it makes sense, but...

00:09:14.054 --> 00:09:16.723
But what?

00:09:18.559 --> 00:09:21.061
No, never mind.

00:09:21.061 --> 00:09:24.565
What's the problem?
If you got a complaint, I'll listen.

00:09:24.565 --> 00:09:26.650
--Come on, tell me.
--It's okay.

00:09:26.650 --> 00:09:30.070
Spit it out!
You'll feel a lot better.

00:09:33.323 --> 00:09:35.075
I haven't seen him before.

00:09:39.663 --> 00:09:41.123
Water, please.

00:09:41.123 --> 00:09:43.292
Idiot. Order some alcohol.

00:09:43.292 --> 00:09:46.086
I don't want alcohol.
I'll have water.

00:09:46.086 --> 00:09:47.629
Whatever...

00:09:53.010 --> 00:09:55.012
Uh, excuse me,
First Lieutenant.

00:09:55.012 --> 00:09:59.016
I really hate to come off
like a tight-ass, but...

00:09:59.016 --> 00:10:01.101
could you move to another seat?

00:10:01.101 --> 00:10:02.394
Why's that?

00:10:02.394 --> 00:10:09.151
These three seats are humbly reserved
for us in the SRT, the Special Response Team.

00:10:09.151 --> 00:10:11.570
And you're sitting in one of them.

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:13.780
Is that one of the regulations?

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:16.825
The guys at the base
just decided it on their own.

00:10:16.825 --> 00:10:22.164
But yeah, I guess you could
call those seats reserved, kid.

00:10:22.164 --> 00:10:24.082
I have no idea what you mean.

00:10:24.082 --> 00:10:27.920
That's the seat our dead
superior officer used to sit at.

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:32.257
Sorry, but we don't want your ass sitting there
when we've never even seen you before.

00:10:32.257 --> 00:10:34.134
I see.

00:10:36.762 --> 00:10:40.307
What were the name and call sign
of your dead superior officer?

00:10:40.307 --> 00:10:43.727
Uruz 1, Gail McAllen.

00:10:43.727 --> 00:10:46.230
Then I don't need to change seats.

00:10:46.230 --> 00:10:48.148
That man was a coward.

00:10:50.484 --> 00:10:53.695
Umm... Coward?

00:10:53.695 --> 00:10:56.156
Did you just say "coward"?

00:10:56.156 --> 00:10:58.825
That's right. He was incompetent.

00:10:58.825 --> 00:11:00.369
Wow.

00:11:00.369 --> 00:11:02.037
You sure come on strong, don't you?

00:11:02.037 --> 00:11:04.831
Did you hear that? He called
Lieutenant McAllen "incompetent."

00:11:04.831 --> 00:11:08.627
But you know, he sure was...

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:16.260
Kurz!

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:19.763
Your endurance stinks, Sergeant.

00:11:19.763 --> 00:11:21.223
Frickin' asshole...

00:11:21.223 --> 00:11:22.641
I'm fired up now!

00:11:26.186 --> 00:11:27.104
Kurz!

00:11:27.104 --> 00:11:30.148
Leave him alone.
It's just a light concussion.

00:11:30.148 --> 00:11:33.277
I'm surprised he could stand up
after taking that punch, but...

00:11:33.277 --> 00:11:36.113
Judging from that sergeant
and the dead lieutenant,

00:11:36.113 --> 00:11:38.490
it looks like the entire
SRT here is a bunch of dolts.

00:11:38.490 --> 00:11:41.535
I'm disappointed.

00:11:41.535 --> 00:11:43.161
You look like you want
to say something.

00:11:43.161 --> 00:11:46.331
First Lieutenant, I apologize
for my comrade's rudeness.

00:11:46.331 --> 00:11:50.419
But I'd like you to take back your
insult toward Lieutenant McAllen.

00:11:50.419 --> 00:11:52.379
And if I say no?

00:11:53.213 --> 00:11:54.673
What's the matter?

00:11:54.673 --> 00:11:57.801
Are you going to get into a fist fight
with a superior officer like this dolt here?

00:11:57.801 --> 00:11:59.428
You can't, can you?

00:11:59.428 --> 00:12:01.722
You appear to be a serious man.

00:12:01.722 --> 00:12:04.141
But you can't do anything
without an order.

00:12:04.141 --> 00:12:06.810
In a way, you're a kind of coward.

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:09.771
Do you need an excuse
to vindicate yourself?

00:12:09.771 --> 00:12:12.774
Then how about this, Sergeant?
Do you want to try a little game?

00:12:12.774 --> 00:12:16.236
You want to defend
McAllen's honor, don't you?

00:12:16.236 --> 00:12:20.490
I was just feeling bored, myself.
Come with me. And that's an order.

00:12:29.249 --> 00:12:30.667
Hmm?

00:12:31.835 --> 00:12:34.463
What do you want?
Did you come to laugh at me?

00:12:34.463 --> 00:12:36.590
I came to deliver
replacement machines.

00:12:36.590 --> 00:12:38.300
M types.

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:40.844
You came all the way
here just for that?

00:12:40.844 --> 00:12:44.598
Actually, there's something
I'd like to discuss with you.

00:12:44.598 --> 00:12:46.808
It's about those sisters.

00:12:46.808 --> 00:12:50.562
I have an idea of what
those girls intend to do.

00:12:50.562 --> 00:12:52.523
I'd like you to stop them,
if possible.

00:12:52.523 --> 00:12:55.484
Just shut up and watch.

00:12:55.484 --> 00:12:56.610
Understood.

00:12:56.610 --> 00:12:58.278
So that's how it is.

00:12:58.278 --> 00:13:00.280
I will go along with your style.

00:13:02.366 --> 00:13:03.992
Splendid.

00:13:03.992 --> 00:13:08.205
I'm going to have to punish
those mischievous kittens good.

00:13:26.390 --> 00:13:27.307
Yes?

00:13:27.307 --> 00:13:28.559
It's me.

00:13:28.559 --> 00:13:30.435
You've seen her?

00:13:30.435 --> 00:13:31.562
Yeah.

00:13:31.562 --> 00:13:32.521
Well?

00:13:32.521 --> 00:13:34.982
We can kill her.
Any time.

00:13:34.982 --> 00:13:37.526
Then wait for the order.

00:13:37.526 --> 00:13:38.652
Yeah.

00:13:38.652 --> 00:13:40.445
Is Sensei okay?

00:13:40.445 --> 00:13:43.282
Yes. For a little while.

00:13:43.282 --> 00:13:44.825
See you.

00:13:48.745 --> 00:13:50.455
Sensei.

00:13:50.455 --> 00:13:52.416
We are about to begin.

00:13:58.046 --> 00:13:59.798
<i>A game?</i>

00:13:59.798 --> 00:14:01.925
<i>He calls this a game?</i>

00:14:07.181 --> 00:14:10.017
That machine is the same one as then...

00:14:10.017 --> 00:14:12.311
A unit identical to the M9 type.

00:14:12.311 --> 00:14:13.979
It's a D series experimental machine.

00:14:13.979 --> 00:14:17.649
The specs are not significantly different
from those of the current E series.

00:14:17.649 --> 00:14:20.861
Now that I think about it, I haven't
properly introduced myself yet, have I?

00:14:20.861 --> 00:14:23.030
I've just transferred from
the Mediterranean Sea Fleet.

00:14:23.030 --> 00:14:25.574
First Lieutenant Belfangan Clouseau.

00:14:25.574 --> 00:14:30.913
As of today, I've been assigned
to the West Pacific Ocean Fleet's SRT.

00:14:30.913 --> 00:14:33.415
My call sign is Uruz 1.

00:14:33.415 --> 00:14:36.877
In other words,
I'm your team leader.

00:14:36.877 --> 00:14:38.295
But there's no need to hold back.

00:14:38.295 --> 00:14:42.341
Use that AS to prove to me
that my predecessor wasn't incompetent.

00:14:43.592 --> 00:14:44.843
Here we go.

00:14:47.387 --> 00:14:48.388
<i>Bastard...</i>

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:52.893
Your power is the same as mine. And...

00:15:02.528 --> 00:15:04.404
...your techniques aren't bad, either.

00:15:04.404 --> 00:15:05.364
But...

00:15:07.282 --> 00:15:07.950
What?!

00:15:16.083 --> 00:15:17.417
<i>He's strong.</i>

00:15:17.417 --> 00:15:20.420
Just like I thought,
you're a second-rate operator.

00:15:20.420 --> 00:15:22.506
Your fighting method has skill,

00:15:22.506 --> 00:15:25.425
but it isn't art.

00:15:25.425 --> 00:15:28.428
Do you understand the difference?

00:15:28.428 --> 00:15:31.098
I guess playing around like this
won't show me anything.

00:15:31.098 --> 00:15:34.434
We've got the opportunity.
Why don't we have a serious fight?

00:15:34.434 --> 00:15:35.435
Warning.

00:15:35.435 --> 00:15:38.605
Alpha 1 has started
its monomolecular cutter.

00:15:38.605 --> 00:15:39.773
<i>Is he serious?</i>

00:15:39.773 --> 00:15:40.524
Let's go!

00:15:42.025 --> 00:15:42.818
That's it!

00:15:54.663 --> 00:15:57.875
I don't admire this kind of method.

00:15:57.875 --> 00:16:00.085
His name is First Lieutenant Clouseau, correct?

00:16:00.085 --> 00:16:01.879
He makes strange propositions.

00:16:01.879 --> 00:16:03.672
I am the one who gave permission.

00:16:03.672 --> 00:16:04.840
Because if we don't do this,

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:08.093
he probably won't be able to draw out
the Arbalest's fundamental power.

00:16:08.093 --> 00:16:10.512
Then it is not of any use in battle.

00:16:10.512 --> 00:16:14.141
Being able to depend on it
to activate reliably when needed:

00:16:14.141 --> 00:16:17.144
<i>that </i>is the very life of a weapon system.

00:16:17.144 --> 00:16:19.479
Are you saying the Arbalest is defective?

00:16:19.479 --> 00:16:23.025
Yes, ma'am. I do not like that machine at all.

00:16:23.025 --> 00:16:25.694
Sergeant Sagara probably feels the same way.

00:16:25.694 --> 00:16:27.362
That's the problem.

00:16:43.170 --> 00:16:44.171
Dammit.

00:16:44.171 --> 00:16:47.549
Ugly. Butt-ugly.

00:16:47.549 --> 00:16:50.844
You're awkward and overbearing
and don't have one shred of flexibility.

00:16:50.844 --> 00:16:52.346
Get up, Sergeant.

00:16:52.346 --> 00:16:54.556
Try drawing out every bit
of power that machine has.

00:16:54.556 --> 00:16:56.683
Understood?
Every last bit of it!

00:16:56.683 --> 00:16:58.435
Every bit of it?

00:17:02.231 --> 00:17:03.774
The Lambda Driver?

00:17:03.774 --> 00:17:05.108
Let's go, Sergeant!

00:17:06.568 --> 00:17:08.779
But it...

00:17:08.779 --> 00:17:09.947
It...

00:17:27.589 --> 00:17:30.676
So you're just a pet
dog after all, huh?

00:17:32.553 --> 00:17:34.388
Looks like it's over.

00:17:34.388 --> 00:17:36.849
The Lambda Driver did not activate.

00:17:36.849 --> 00:17:38.684
I can see that.

00:17:41.436 --> 00:17:43.021
Idiot.

00:17:52.573 --> 00:17:56.618
So you were going to get revenge on this guy
and he beat you easy, huh? How pathetic.

00:18:05.294 --> 00:18:07.629
Neither one of you got punished.

00:18:07.629 --> 00:18:10.299
Looks like the whole thing
was just a farce.

00:18:10.299 --> 00:18:12.634
So that's what it was, huh?

00:18:14.136 --> 00:18:17.723
You're finally awake, huh?

00:18:17.723 --> 00:18:19.183
Sergeant Sagara.

00:18:19.183 --> 00:18:22.060
Do you understand why you were beaten?

00:18:22.060 --> 00:18:23.270
The difference in our skill.

00:18:23.270 --> 00:18:24.438
Wrong.

00:18:24.438 --> 00:18:26.481
It's a more basic reason.

00:18:26.481 --> 00:18:29.151
Something fatal that you can't bury
no matter how much skill you have.

00:18:29.151 --> 00:18:31.111
I don't understand what you mean.

00:18:31.111 --> 00:18:33.614
You detest the Arbalest.

00:18:34.990 --> 00:18:37.159
I could tell as soon as we fought.

00:18:37.159 --> 00:18:41.622
Your step, your arm movement,
every one of your attacks...

00:18:41.622 --> 00:18:43.790
They all had doubt in them.

00:18:43.790 --> 00:18:45.459
They had impatience.

00:18:45.459 --> 00:18:47.252
They didn't have any heart.

00:18:47.252 --> 00:18:52.174
Never mind about the Lambda Driver,
this problem runs even deeper.

00:18:52.174 --> 00:18:55.636
First Lieutenant.
The attack you used to bring me down...

00:18:55.636 --> 00:18:59.556
You think I used a
Lambda Driver to pull it off?

00:18:59.556 --> 00:19:04.937
Sorry to say this, but it doesn't take
a Lambda Driver to beat you and the Arbalest.

00:19:04.937 --> 00:19:09.608
It was a technique that combines what
the Japanese would call "toshi" and "sunkei."

00:19:09.608 --> 00:19:15.781
The M9 is capable of that much potential,
depending on the operator.

00:19:15.781 --> 00:19:17.741
Listen up, Sergeant.

00:19:17.741 --> 00:19:22.287
The weapon we use, the AS,
isn't just a machine.

00:19:22.287 --> 00:19:25.874
It's an extension
of the trained soldier's body!

00:19:25.874 --> 00:19:29.211
The heart of the operator
is reflected in the machine.

00:19:29.211 --> 00:19:34.258
In a high-level battle, that small difference
determines whether you win or lose.

00:19:34.258 --> 00:19:37.010
Realize that a man who can't
even trust his own body

00:19:37.010 --> 00:19:40.347
has no hope of beating the enemies
we'll be up against from now on.

00:19:40.347 --> 00:19:41.765
That is all.

00:19:43.183 --> 00:19:45.185
How long do you plan on
just sitting there?

00:19:45.185 --> 00:19:47.354
Go to the hangar
and give your signature.

00:19:47.354 --> 00:19:48.605
I expect a report too.

00:19:48.605 --> 00:19:50.691
Starting tomorrow,
I'm going to thoroughly re-train you.

00:19:50.691 --> 00:19:52.860
Weber, you too.

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:54.486
Yeah, yeah.

00:19:57.197 --> 00:20:00.242
The new guy's one nasty bastard.

00:20:00.242 --> 00:20:01.660
But he's strong.

00:20:03.245 --> 00:20:04.913
He completely defeated me.

00:20:17.509 --> 00:20:19.178
It was you, wasn't it?

00:20:19.178 --> 00:20:21.805
That's right.

00:20:21.805 --> 00:20:23.932
It's been, what, a year and a half?

00:20:23.932 --> 00:20:27.936
Actually, it's been 5 days.
We saw each other in Sicily.

00:20:27.936 --> 00:20:29.855
Was this his room?

00:20:29.855 --> 00:20:33.066
Yeah. It was Lieutenant McAllen's room.

00:20:34.401 --> 00:20:36.987
Did he suffer?

00:20:36.987 --> 00:20:39.072
They said it was instantaneous.

00:20:39.072 --> 00:20:40.949
I see.

00:20:40.949 --> 00:20:43.744
About that Sagara guy...

00:20:43.744 --> 00:20:46.288
He's exactly like I used to be.

00:20:46.288 --> 00:20:51.293
He's trying to act tough, blindly trying
to force himself to fit into a certain frame.

00:20:51.293 --> 00:20:55.297
Even though if he wanted to,
he could make that frame bigger.

00:20:55.297 --> 00:20:57.549
Can he learn to do that?

00:20:57.549 --> 00:20:58.800
I don't know.

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:01.887
But if he stays like this, he'll probably die.

00:21:01.887 --> 00:21:04.765
Or, he could turn into a real loser.

00:21:04.765 --> 00:21:06.266
Loser?

00:21:06.266 --> 00:21:10.062
I'm talking about the guys
we're fighting all the time.

00:21:10.062 --> 00:21:12.689
Malice builds up slowly.

00:21:12.689 --> 00:21:16.276
First, you lie to yourself.
Then, you resent the people around you.

00:21:16.276 --> 00:21:19.696
And last, you begin
to scorn the entire world.

00:21:19.696 --> 00:21:21.323
It all happens gradually.

00:21:21.323 --> 00:21:24.076
It's a very slow change,
like the hour hand on a clock.

00:21:24.076 --> 00:21:26.245
That's what makes it so frightening.

00:21:27.746 --> 00:21:30.791
I'm beat. I'm going to bed.

00:21:33.794 --> 00:21:35.254
Melissa.

00:21:35.254 --> 00:21:36.713
What?

00:21:36.713 --> 00:21:40.008
Don't tell anyone that the
lieutenant and I were war buddies.

00:21:40.008 --> 00:21:43.428
I don't want them to think
they have to tip-toe around me.

00:21:43.428 --> 00:21:45.222
As you wish.

00:21:45.222 --> 00:21:47.099
Goodnight, Ben.

00:21:50.811 --> 00:21:52.980
Captain. May I have a word?

00:21:52.980 --> 00:21:54.106
What is it?

00:21:54.106 --> 00:21:57.109
A D Standby order from Tactical Headquarters.

00:21:57.109 --> 00:21:59.820
An AS unit is causing large-scale destruction.

00:21:59.820 --> 00:22:02.030
They are currently carrying out
the response procedure.

00:22:02.030 --> 00:22:02.948
What's the location?

00:22:02.948 --> 00:22:04.449
It's Hong Kong.

00:22:27.764 --> 00:22:33.312
<i>Kitto kimi wa kyou no hi mo</i>

00:22:33.312 --> 00:22:39.193
<i>Massugu ashita wo miteru</i>

00:22:39.193 --> 00:22:44.907
<i>Kaze ga fuku ano oka ni saita</i>

00:22:44.907 --> 00:22:51.663
<i>himawari no you ni</i>

00:22:53.582 --> 00:22:59.505
<i>Donna ni tooku hanareteite mo</i>

00:22:59.505 --> 00:23:05.511
<i>Kono utagoe ga kimi ni todoku you ni</i>

00:23:05.511 --> 00:23:11.558
<i>Namida ga zutto tomaranai yoru</i>

00:23:11.558 --> 00:23:17.898
<i>Kimi no mado wo terasu tsuki ni naritai</i>

00:23:17.898 --> 00:23:25.948
<i>Mata kanarazu aeru to</i>

00:23:28.283 --> 00:23:31.870
<i>Sou omou kara</i>

00:23:45.133 --> 00:23:46.009
"Next Episode"

00:23:46.009 --> 00:23:50.389
<i>Left behind in Tokyo,</i>
<i>Chidori had begun a lonely battle.</i>

00:23:50.389 --> 00:23:51.974
<i>Loneliness and doubt.</i>

00:23:51.974 --> 00:23:54.101
<i>The gaze of an invisible watcher</i>
<i>causes her fear to grow.</i>

00:23:54.101 --> 00:23:56.103
<i>She can't trust anyone anymore.</i>

00:23:56.103 --> 00:23:58.605
<i>Next time: "Her Problem."</i>

00:23:58.605 --> 00:24:04.715
<i>One war ends,</i>
<i>like tears disappearing in the rain...</i>
